---
import '../styles/landing.css';

const repo = 'https://github.com/eshlox/dvm';
const title = 'DVM - Disposable development VMs';
const description =
  'A small Bash wrapper around Lima for disposable development VMs. No host mounts, your own setup scripts, a clean host machine.';

// Entirely fictional. Any resemblance to real engineers is the joke.
const testimonials = [
  { quote: "I broke everything inside the VM, deleted it, and felt absolutely nothing. This is the closure my Dockerfiles never gave me.", who: "Dependency H.", role: "Recovering YAML Engineer" },
  { quote: "My laptop fans haven't spun up since I switched. My cat is unsettled by the silence.", who: "A. Nonymous", role: "Staff Procrastinator" },
  { quote: "Finally, a tool that respects boundaries better than my last three side projects did.", who: "Jane Doe-Notexist", role: "Principal Vibes Architect" },
  { quote: "I <code>dvm rm</code>'d production. Kidding, there is no production. That's the entire point.", who: "Seg Fault", role: "CTO of a company I invented for this quote" },
  { quote: "I used to pipe curl straight into sudo bash. Now I do it inside a VM I can throw away. Personal growth.", who: "Rm Dashrf", role: "Senior Move Fast Engineer" },
  { quote: "My threat model used to be 'it works on my machine'. Now my machine is disposable, so checkmate.", who: "Bobby Tables", role: "Database Enthusiast" },
  { quote: "I ran a sketchy install script with 4,000 stars and zero reviews. The VM died so my laptop didn't have to.", who: "Yolo Driven", role: "Lead Optimist" },
  { quote: "Security asked where I run untrusted code. I pointed at a VM I delete every afternoon. They wept. Happy tears, I assume.", who: "Patch Tuesday", role: "Compliance Avoider" },
  { quote: "I no longer read the install script. I just make sure it can't reach my SSH keys. We call this maturity.", who: "Copy Paste", role: "Stack Overflow Archaeologist" },
  { quote: "I gave node_modules its own quarantine wing. It has earned nothing less.", who: "N. P. M", role: "Dependency Hoarder" },
  { quote: "It's like a hotel room for my code. I trash it, check out, and leave no forwarding address.", who: "Vim Exiteer", role: "Modal Editor Survivor" },
  { quote: "Spun up a VM to test one regex. Worth it. The regex still doesn't work, but my host is pristine.", who: "Greedy Match", role: "Backtracking Specialist" },
  { quote: "I containerized my containers and then put them in a VM. My therapist and I are working through it.", who: "Kube Nettes", role: "Over-Engineer in Residence" },
  { quote: "Zero host mounts means zero 'why is there a node_modules in my home directory' moments.", who: "Tilde Slash", role: "Filesystem Janitor" },
  { quote: "I finally have a sandbox that isn't just /tmp and a prayer.", who: "Temp File", role: "Reckless Tester" },
  { quote: "It boots faster than my standup ends, and is roughly as disposable.", who: "Daily Scrum", role: "Agile Skeptic" },
  { quote: "I read the whole man page. Then I read it again. I have no notes. I am shaken.", who: "RTF Manual", role: "Documentation Believer" },
  { quote: "My git history is a crime scene, but at least my host machine is clean.", who: "Force Push", role: "Friday Deployer" },
  { quote: "Spin up. Break stuff. Delete. Repeat. It's basically meditation.", who: "Ohm Resolver", role: "Mindful Engineer" },
  { quote: "I trust nothing and I mount nothing. We are the same.", who: "Air Gap", role: "Paranoid Architect" },
  { quote: "Ten out of ten. Would dispose again.", who: "Five Stars", role: "Professional Reviewer" },
  { quote: "It does one thing and flatly refuses to do my taxes. Respect.", who: "Scope Creep", role: "Feature Requester" },
  { quote: "I came for the isolation. I stayed because I forgot I had other tabs open.", who: "Lost Focus", role: "Context Switcher" },
  { quote: "Faster than reading the Dockerfile I copied from a 2019 blog post.", who: "Cache Hit", role: "Latency Connoisseur" },
  { quote: "My VM has better boundaries than my calendar.", who: "Always Available", role: "Burned Out Lead" },
  { quote: "I store secrets in env vars, in the VM, which I then delete. The secrets get deleted too. Nobody warned me.", who: "Plain Text", role: "Senior Oops Engineer" },
  { quote: "I used to test in prod. Now I test in a VM that merely thinks it's prod. Therapy is going great.", who: "Hotfix Hank", role: "Incident Commander" },
  { quote: "My password is still 'password', but the blast radius is one disposable VM now.", who: "Auth Zero", role: "Identity Crisis" },
  { quote: "I disabled the firewall, SELinux, and my better judgment. The VM forgave all of it on delete.", who: "Setenforce Zero", role: "Hardening Skeptic" },
  { quote: "Someone said 'supply chain attack' and I said 'not my host's problem anymore'.", who: "Lockfile Larry", role: "npm install --force" },
  { quote: "I ran the malware in the VM on purpose. For science. The science was: yep, that's malware.", who: "Curious George", role: "Reverse Engineer, Allegedly" },
  { quote: "I don't sanitize inputs, but I do sanitize my entire VM by deleting it. Net positive.", who: "Little Bobby", role: "Returning Character" },
  { quote: "It's the only thing in my workflow that does exactly what the README claims.", who: "Honest Readme", role: "Rare Specimen" },
  { quote: "I named my VMs after my regrets. Spinning up 'the-rewrite' was unexpectedly cathartic.", who: "Tech Debt", role: "Interest, Compounding" },
  { quote: "My CI went green for the first time because I tested in a clean room before pushing.", who: "Flaky Test", role: "Reformed" },
  { quote: "I gave up on perfect dotfiles. Now every VM gets the precise chaos it deserves, freshly.", who: "Chez Moi", role: "Config Drifter" },
  { quote: "It quietly logs everything and shows me a checkmark. It is more emotionally available than I am.", who: "Spinner Loading", role: "Async Person" },
  { quote: "I uninstalled my anxiety and reinstalled it as a VM I can delete.", who: "Heap Overflow", role: "Memory Leaker" },
  { quote: "Works on my machine, and also on the disposable machine, which is the only machine I trust now.", who: "It Compiles", role: "Ship It Advocate" },
  { quote: "I read 'no host mounts' and a single tear of joy rolled into my mechanical keyboard.", who: "Cherry MX", role: "Clack Evangelist" },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://dvm.eshlox.net/" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://dvm.eshlox.net/" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <script is:inline>
      // Apply the theme chosen in the docs (Starlight stores it) before paint.
      // 'auto'/unset falls through to the prefers-color-scheme media query.
      (function () {
        try {
          var t = localStorage.getItem('starlight-theme');
          if (t === 'light' || t === 'dark') document.documentElement.dataset.theme = t;
        } catch (e) {}
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <body class="landing">
    <!-- nav -->
    <nav class="nav">
      <a class="brand" href="/">
        <img src="/favicon.svg" alt="" />
        <span>DVM</span>
      </a>
      <div class="nav-links">
        <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
        <a href="/docs/examples/">Examples</a>
        <a href={repo}>GitHub</a>
        <button id="theme-toggle" class="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Toggle color theme">
          <svg class="icon-moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M21 12.8A9 9 0 1 1 11.2 3a7 7 0 0 0 9.8 9.8Z" />
          </svg>
          <svg class="icon-sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4" />
            <path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4" />
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- hero -->
    <header class="hero wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Bash · Lima 2.0+</span>
      <h1>Disposable dev VMs.<br /><span class="grad">Zero host footprint.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A small Bash wrapper around Lima. Spin up a clean VM, run your own setup
        scripts, build whatever you want, then throw it away. Nothing from your
        machine is mounted into the guest.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/">Get started →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
      </div>
      <div class="install mono">
        <span class="dollar">$</span>
        <span id="install-cmd">git clone https://github.com/eshlox/dvm.git &amp;&amp; cd dvm &amp;&amp; ./install.sh</span>
        <button id="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy install command">copy</button>
      </div>

      <!-- terminal demo -->
      <div class="term-shell mono" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="term-bar">
          <span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span>
          <span class="title">dvm - quickstart</span>
        </div>
        <div class="term-body">
          <div class="line"><span class="ps">$ </span><span class="cmd">dvm new app</span></div>
          <div class="line out">wrote ~/.config/dvm/vms/app/&#123;config.sh,setup.sh&#125;</div>
          <div class="spacer"></div>
          <div class="line"><span class="ps">$ </span><span class="cmd">dvm sync app</span></div>
          <div class="line ok">✓ creating instance dvm-app</div>
          <div class="line ok">✓ ensuring user "dev" and ~/code/app</div>
          <div class="line ok">✓ running global setup</div>
          <div class="line ok">✓ app ready</div>
          <div class="spacer"></div>
          <div class="line"><span class="ps">$ </span><span class="cmd">dvm sh app</span></div>
          <div class="line"><span class="out">dev@app</span><span class="ps">:~/code/app$ </span><span class="cursor"></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- features -->
    <section class="features wrap">
      <h2>Built to stay out of your way</h2>
      <p class="sub">Sensible, secure defaults. Everything project-specific lives in scripts you own.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="ico">⊘</div>
          <h3>No host mounts</h3>
          <p>By default nothing from your machine is shared into the guest. Your files stay yours.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="ico">❯</div>
          <h3>Your setup, your scripts</h3>
          <p>Provisioning is plain Bash you write and review. Tool installation lives in setup scripts, not in DVM.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="ico">✓</div>
          <h3>Checked before they run</h3>
          <p>Setup scripts are ownership- and permission-checked before DVM will execute them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="ico">⎈</div>
          <h3>Per-VM dev user</h3>
          <p>Each VM gets its own user and a tidy <code>~/code/&lt;vm&gt;</code> workspace, isolated per project.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="ico">◔</div>
          <h3>Dry-run first</h3>
          <p><code>DVM_DRY_RUN=1</code> prints the Lima argv and setup order without touching Lima at all.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="ico">♺</div>
          <h3>Disposable by design</h3>
          <p>One command to build, one to destroy. Break things freely, then start fresh.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- testimonials (fake, and honest about it) -->
    <section class="testimonials wrap">
      <h2>What developers are saying</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        These are completely made up, because nobody real has said anything yet.
        Want to be the first? <a href={`${repo}/discussions`}>Tell me what you think</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="grid">
        {testimonials.map((t) => (
          <figure class="quote">
            <blockquote set:html={`&ldquo;${t.quote}&rdquo;`} />
            <figcaption><span class="who">{t.who}</span><span class="role">{t.role}</span></figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="disclaimer">* No developers were consulted in the making of these {testimonials.length} testimonials.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- bottom cta -->
    <section class="wrap">
      <div class="bottom-cta">
        <h2>Spin up. Build. Throw away.</h2>
        <p>Four commands from nothing to a clean, disposable development VM.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/">Get started →</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={repo}>View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- footer -->
    <footer class="foot">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span>© DVM · MIT License</span>
        <span class="links">
          <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
          <a href="/docs/guides/security/">Security</a>
          <a href={repo}>GitHub</a>
        </span>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <script is:inline>
      // Theme toggle: flips to an explicit theme and persists it the way the
      // docs (Starlight) do, so the choice carries across the whole site.
      const themeToggle = document.getElementById('theme-toggle');
      themeToggle?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const root = document.documentElement;
        const current =
          root.dataset.theme ||
          (matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches ? 'light' : 'dark');
        const next = current === 'light' ? 'dark' : 'light';
        root.dataset.theme = next;
        try {
          localStorage.setItem('starlight-theme', next);
        } catch (e) {}
      });

      const btn = document.getElementById('copy-btn');
      btn?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const cmd = document.getElementById('install-cmd')?.textContent ?? '';
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(cmd);
          const prev = btn.textContent;
          btn.textContent = 'copied';
          setTimeout(() => (btn.textContent = prev), 1400);
        } catch {}
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
